{
 "thread": "kpkKWTvoEks",
 "subject": "Parameter matrices with a mixture of fixed and free parameter values",
 "messages_listed": 5,
 "last_activity": "2016-02-07T21:07:47Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "iBIbLBb0BAAJ",
   "from": "James Savage",
   "author": "29ce8550baceaeb0",
   "date": "2016-02-06T13:00:31Z",
   "subject": "Parameter matrices with a mixture of fixed and free parameter values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all, <div><br></div><div>A common tool in economics is the structural VAR, which uses hard constraints on elements of the VAR coefficient and covariance matrices to help identify an economic model (I&#39;m using &quot;identify&quot; in the economics sense here, as in, loosely, &quot;pin down the causal relationships&quot;). For instance, take a very simple toy model with Y(t) = (USGDP_growth(t), Australan_GDP_growth(t), Australian_unemployment(t))&#39; and specification </div><div><br></div><div>Y(t) ~ multi_normal(A + BY(t-1),  Sigma)</div><div><br></div><div>where A and B are coefficient matrices (no contemporaneous effects). From an economic perspective, it won&#39;t make sense to let B be freely estimated. We&#39;d expect the US economy to exert an effect on the Australian economy (1/15th the size), but not visa versa. Yet US and Australian economic performance will be correlated and an unrestricted estimate of B will say that Australian economic output affects US economic output when we run shocks through the model. </div><div><br></div><div>Ideally, I&#39;d want to do something like</div><div><br></div><div>parameters{</div><div>matrix[3, 3] B;</div><div>B[1,2] &lt;- 0;</div><div>B[1,3] &lt;- 0;</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>Instead I&#39;m doing something like</div><div><br></div><div><div>transformed parameters {</div><div>  matrix[3,3] B1;</div><div>  for(i in 1:3){</div><div>    for(j in 1:3){</div><div>    if(i==1 &amp;&amp; j==2){</div><div>      B1[i,j] &lt;- 0;</div><div>    }</div><div>    if(i==1 &amp;&amp; j ==3){</div><div>      B1[i,j] &lt;- 0;</div><div>    }</div><div>    else {</div><div>      B1[i,j] &lt;- B[i,j];</div><div>    }</div><div>  }}</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div>In which case I&#39;m declaring parameters (in B) that don&#39;t get used in the model. Is this going to be a problem? </div><div><br></div><div>Another option would be to provide very tight priors over the relevant elements of B. I don&#39;t personally object to this, though it&#39;s not standard. </div><div><br></div><div>(Note I&#39;ve not implemented one of these models in Stan yet, but I am considering a large project and I&#39;m trying to think through the potential issues). </div><div><br></div><div>Cheers, </div><div>Jim</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "NZWtgJr1BAAJ",
   "from": "Michael Betancourt",
   "author": "a5e83218c834e013",
   "date": "2016-02-06T13:28:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Parameter matrices with a mixture of fixed and free parameter values",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">In which case I&#39;m declaring parameters (in B) that don&#39;t get used in the model. Is this going to be a problem? </div></blockquote><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div>It won’t technically lead to sampling problems provided that the unused parameters have</div><div>well-posed priors, in which case you reduce to sampling from those priors.</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:11px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">(Note I&#39;ve not implemented one of these models in Stan yet, but I am considering a large project and I&#39;m trying to think through the potential issues). </div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div></div><br><div>The reason why this seems awkward is because it is!  When you want to impose causal</div><div>constraints like this you need to impose generative structure in your model, not hack</div><div>stochastic structure.  That would mean building an explicit model for the Australian </div><div>economy as a function of the American economy.  Of course this can be anathema</div><div>to economists so you might be in between awkward hacks and fighting conventions...</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "EbIru0H2BAAJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2016-02-06T13:40:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: Parameter matrices with a mixture of fixed and free parameter values",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On Saturday, February 6, 2016 at 8:00:31 AM UTC-5, James Savage wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Ideally, I&#39;d want to do something like<div><br></div><div>parameters{</div><div>matrix[3, 3] B;</div><div>B[1,2] &lt;- 0;</div><div>B[1,3] &lt;- 0;</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>Instead I&#39;m doing something like</div><div><br></div><div><div>transformed parameters {</div><div>  matrix[3,3] B1;</div><div>  for(i in 1:3){</div><div>    for(j in 1:3){</div><div>    if(i==1 &amp;&amp; j==2){</div><div>      B1[i,j] &lt;- 0;</div><div>    }</div><div>    if(i==1 &amp;&amp; j ==3){</div><div>      B1[i,j] &lt;- 0;</div><div>    }</div><div>    else {</div><div>      B1[i,j] &lt;- B[i,j];</div><div>    }</div><div>  }}</div><div>}</div></div><div><br></div><div>In which case I&#39;m declaring parameters (in B) that don&#39;t get used in the model. Is this going to be a problem? </div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>I would declare a parameter vector and transform it into a matrix<span style=\"color:#000\"></span> using the new slicing assignment syntax:<br><span style=\"color:#000\"></span><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">transformed data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// you could also pass these in as data</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lower</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">upper</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Bvec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">row_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">col_mark</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Bvec</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div></div></code></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>Ben<br><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
