  {
   "id": "Ttry8h-jAAAJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2016-02-07T21:07:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-users] Parameter matrices with a mixture of fixed and free parameter values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Nice.  This is going into the manual:\r<br>\r<br><a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1709#issuecomment-181116697\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1709%23issuecomment-181116697&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462598358000&amp;usg=AOvVaw13VkjMoc0K10nc9-LLwk8U\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1709#issuecomment-181116697</a>\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>&gt; On Feb 6, 2016, at 8:40 AM, Ben Goodrich &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Saturday, February 6, 2016 at 8:00:31 AM UTC-5, James Savage wrote:\r<br>&gt; Ideally, I&#39;d want to do something like\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; parameters{\r<br>&gt; matrix[3, 3] B;\r<br>&gt; B[1,2] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt; B[1,3] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Instead I&#39;m doing something like\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; transformed parameters {\r<br>&gt;   matrix[3,3] B1;\r<br>&gt;   for(i in 1:3){\r<br>&gt;     for(j in 1:3){\r<br>&gt;     if(i==1 &amp;&amp; j==2){\r<br>&gt;       B1[i,j] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt;     if(i==1 &amp;&amp; j ==3){\r<br>&gt;       B1[i,j] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt;     else {\r<br>&gt;       B1[i,j] &lt;- B[i,j];\r<br>&gt;     }\r<br>&gt;   }}\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; In which case I&#39;m declaring parameters (in B) that don&#39;t get used in the model. Is this going to be a problem? \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I would declare a parameter vector and transform it into a matrix using the new slicing assignment syntax:\r<br>&gt; transformed data { // you could also pass these in as data\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=1,upper=3&gt; row_mark[7];\r<br>&gt;   int&lt;lower=1,upper=3&gt; col_mark[7];\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[1] &lt;- 1; col_mark[1] &lt;- 1;\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[2] &lt;- 2; col_mark[2] &lt;- 1;\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[3] &lt;- 3; col_mark[3] &lt;- 1;\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[4] &lt;- 2; col_mark[4] &lt;- 2;\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[5] &lt;- 3; col_mark[5] &lt;- 2;\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[6] &lt;- 2; col_mark[6] &lt;- 3;\r<br>&gt;   row_mark[7] &lt;- 3; col_mark[7] &lt;- 3;\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; parameters {\r<br>&gt;   vector[7] Bvec;\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; model {\r<br>&gt;   matrix[3,3] B;\r<br>&gt;   B[row_mark,col_mark] &lt;- Bvec;\r<br>&gt;   B[1,2] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt;   B[1,3] &lt;- 0;\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Ben\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
